@node probs "Problems which could occur"

The only KNOWN thing is that, DeletedMover looks for the string DELETED, if
it's  found  somewhere  else then instead of the filesize then it'll surely
fuck up your filelist, this will surely be fixed in the future eg:

AMIX36.DOC   D DELETED 12-28-93  AmiExpress v3.6 - DOCZ
^^
This is ok

AMIX36.DOC   D  180000 12-28-93  AmiExpress v3.6 - DELETED STUFF
                                                   ^^^^^^^
                         THIS ENTRY WOULD FUCK UP YOUR FILELIST

Keep also in mind that DELETED has always to be UPPERCASE, eg.:  DELETED is
ok, Deleted or DeLeTeD or something like that will NOT be found.

The  biggest  problem  are  people  who do not read the dox and then set up
things wrong and claim me writing my doors shitty...

@endnode


@node introduction "Introduction - lat.: inter ducere ~ put it in man"
DeletedMover moves files marked with DELETED instead of the filesize from
one filelist to another.

                     IMPORTANT - IMPORTANT - IMPORTANT
The String DELETED MUST BE UPPERCASE (read @{"probs" link probs} for more info)


USAGE: DM SOURCE DESTINATION

Example: DM bbs:conf4/dir2 bbs:conf4/dir1

Moves   all   dexcriptions   marked   as  deleted  from  bbs:conf4/dir2  to
bbs:conf4/dir1, easy ah ???


THIS  IS JUST A BETA RELEASE SO WAIT FOR DA COMPLETE VERSION BEFORE U START
COMPLAINING

@endnode
